{
 "intro": "Practice Python concepts with matching, ordering and fill-in tasks. Everything is graded in your browser.",
 "labs": [
  {
   "id": "py-basics",
   "title": "Python building blocks",
   "domain": "D2",
   "kind": "tasks",
   "level": "beginner",
   "minutes": 10,
   "summary": "Identify data types, complete statements and order a script.",
   "scenario": "<p>You are reviewing a teammate's first script. Show that you can read and finish it.</p>",
   "activities": [
    {
     "type": "match",
     "title": "Value to type",
     "prompt": "Drag each value to its Python type.",
     "categories": [
      "int",
      "float",
      "str",
      "bool",
      "list",
      "dict"
     ],
     "items": [
      {
       "text": "42",
       "cat": 0
      },
      {
       "text": "3.14",
       "cat": 1
      },
      {
       "text": "\"server01\"",
       "cat": 2
      },
      {
       "text": "True",
       "cat": 3
      },
      {
       "text": "[\"web1\", \"web2\"]",
       "cat": 4
      },
      {
       "text": "{\"ip\": \"10.0.0.5\"}",
       "cat": 5
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "fill",
     "title": "Complete the code",
     "prompt": "Type what is missing.",
     "rows": [
      {
       "label": "Keyword that starts a loop over each item",
       "answer": [
        "for"
       ],
       "placeholder": "..."
      },
      {
       "label": "Keyword that defines a function",
       "answer": [
        "def"
       ],
       "placeholder": "..."
      },
      {
       "label": "Comparison operator that tests equality (symbol)",
       "answer": [
        "=="
       ],
       "placeholder": "..."
      },
      {
       "label": "Function that prints to the screen",
       "answer": [
        "print",
        "print()"
       ],
       "placeholder": "..."
      },
      {
       "label": "Method that adds an item to the end of a list",
       "answer": [
        "append",
        ".append",
        ".append()",
        "append()"
       ],
       "placeholder": "..."
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "order",
     "title": "Order a small script",
     "prompt": "Put the steps in a sensible order.",
     "items": [
      "Open the log file with a with block",
      "Loop over each line",
      "Test for the word ERROR",
      "Count the matching lines",
      "Print the total"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "tasks": [
    {
     "text": "Value to type",
     "check": {
      "activity": 0
     }
    },
    {
     "text": "Complete the code",
     "check": {
      "activity": 1
     }
    },
    {
     "text": "Order a small script",
     "check": {
      "activity": 2
     }
    }
   ],
   "hints": [
    "== compares; = assigns.",
    "Open, loop, test, count, print."
   ],
   "review": "<p>Reading code is as important as writing it: know the types, the loop and function keywords, and the flow of a simple log-counting script.</p>"
  },
  {
   "id": "py-automation",
   "title": "Safe automation habits",
   "domain": "D4",
   "kind": "tasks",
   "level": "intermediate",
   "minutes": 12,
   "summary": "Pick the safe approach for each automation task and complete the module names.",
   "scenario": "<p>A script will delete old backups and call an inventory API every night. Review how it is written.</p>",
   "activities": [
    {
     "type": "match",
     "title": "Task to tool",
     "prompt": "Drag each job to the Python tool.",
     "categories": [
      "subprocess",
      "shutil",
      "argparse",
      "logging",
      "requests"
     ],
     "items": [
      {
       "text": "Run the ping command",
       "cat": 0
      },
      {
       "text": "Copy a file to a backup folder",
       "cat": 1
      },
      {
       "text": "Accept a --host option when the script runs",
       "cat": 2
      },
      {
       "text": "Record INFO and ERROR messages to a file",
       "cat": 3
      },
      {
       "text": "Call a web API",
       "cat": 4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "match",
     "title": "Safe or unsafe",
     "prompt": "Is each practice safe?",
     "categories": [
      "Safe",
      "Unsafe"
     ],
     "items": [
      {
       "text": "Read the API token from an environment variable",
       "cat": 0
      },
      {
       "text": "Hard-code the password in the script and commit it",
       "cat": 1
      },
      {
       "text": "Add a --dry-run option before deleting files",
       "cat": 0
      },
      {
       "text": "Build a shell command from user input with shell=True",
       "cat": 1
      },
      {
       "text": "Set a timeout on web requests",
       "cat": 0
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "fill",
     "title": "Module names",
     "prompt": "Type the module.",
     "rows": [
      {
       "label": "Module for JSON data",
       "answer": [
        "json"
       ],
       "placeholder": "..."
      },
      {
       "label": "Module for CSV files",
       "answer": [
        "csv"
       ],
       "placeholder": "..."
      },
      {
       "label": "Module for OS-independent file paths",
       "answer": [
        "pathlib"
       ],
       "placeholder": "..."
      },
      {
       "label": "Module for regular expressions",
       "answer": [
        "re"
       ],
       "placeholder": "..."
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
   "tasks": [
    {
     "text": "Task to tool",
     "check": {
      "activity": 0
     }
    },
    {
     "text": "Safe or unsafe",
     "check": {
      "activity": 1
     }
    },
    {
     "text": "Module names",
     "check": {
      "activity": 2
     }
    }
   ],
   "hints": [
    "Secrets belong outside the code.",
    "A dry run previews without changing anything."
   ],
   "review": "<p>Safe automation keeps secrets out of code, previews destructive actions, logs what happens and avoids shell injection.</p>"
  }
 ]
}